WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:02.208
Hi, welcome back to the Lam Rim.

00:00:02.208 --> 00:00:03.868
This is Geshe Michael Roach.

00:00:03.868 --> 00:00:06.670
And what's that lady thinking about?

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:10.193
Let's go to the Tibetan
text of the Lam Rim.

00:00:10.193 --> 00:00:14.410
ZHES SOGS KYI RIGS PA GCIG
LAS MED PAS RTOGS DKA' LA

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:18.340
It means and if you think about it,

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:21.950
I think we can feel it together

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:25.280
that to really believe in a past life,

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:27.990
it's difficult, it's just difficult.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:31.594
We get wrapped up in this life.

00:00:31.594 --> 00:00:35.202
We're focused on this life,
and this life is so busy.

00:00:35.202 --> 00:00:36.910
There's so many things going on,

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:40.510
and it's so concrete, it's
here, we can't deny it.

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:43.157
Then somebody says, "Well,
did you have a past life?"

00:00:43.157 --> 00:00:44.900
And you're like, "Look, maybe,

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:47.995
I don't have time to think about it now."

00:00:47.995 --> 00:00:52.995
Then, I think all of us,
we avoid difficult ideas.

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:56.180
We don't like to think about

00:00:56.180 --> 00:00:58.850
things that are difficult to figure out.

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:02.760
So I think most of us,
we avoid this question

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:04.730
of did we have a past life?

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:09.703
I have to say that Dharmakirti proved

00:01:11.851 --> 00:01:15.220
that there was a past life.
It was a difficult proof.

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:18.010
There were different parts to it.

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:23.010
But the basic idea is,
something to think about,

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:28.010
is that according to Buddhism

00:01:28.010 --> 00:01:31.210
and according to truth, really,

00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:36.210
life cannot be created from
that which is not alive.

00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:39.310
Life cannot come from

00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:41.980
a cause which is not similar to life.

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:45.530
You don't get apples from pineapples.

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:47.580
What?
That's not so good.

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:51.090
Bananas from rice.

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:53.140
It doesn't happen.

00:01:53.140 --> 00:01:57.040
You don't get awareness of consciousness

00:01:57.040 --> 00:01:59.050
from something other than consciousness.

00:01:59.050 --> 00:02:01.830
That's mainly the whole thing.

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:04.020
That's mainly the whole idea.

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:07.270
What Dharmakirti was saying,

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:09.120
and it was so difficult that I think

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:14.120
maybe we didn't feel it, was
that you can't take a stone

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:16.640
and turn it into life.

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:21.640
Life, there's living flesh
and flesh is imbued with life,

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:25.520
and that flesh comes from chemicals.

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:30.520
But the life part in the
flesh comes from life,

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:34.614
and therefore we must have had life

00:02:34.614 --> 00:02:37.610
just before we were
conceived in this life.

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:39.290
All right so we're...

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:40.123
Here it says

00:02:40.123 --> 00:02:41.973
RIGS PA GCIG LAS MED PAS RTOGS DKA'

00:02:41.973 --> 00:02:45.390
That's where we see the
young lady having difficulty

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:46.540
thinking about...

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:48.448
RTOGS DKA' means look, it's difficult.

00:02:48.448 --> 00:02:51.200
Remember he compared
it to seeing emptiness.

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:55.550
It's on the level of
difficulty of seeing emptiness.

00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:59.871
It's difficult to think,
where did I come from?

00:02:59.871 --> 00:03:04.871
'DI LA DANG PO RIG PA'I YA MTHA'
THUG MED DU BSGRUB DGOS PAS

00:03:05.654 --> 00:03:07.570
This RIG PA, in fact, I corrected it

00:03:07.570 --> 00:03:09.050
and then I uncorrected it.

00:03:09.050 --> 00:03:12.300
This RIG PA does mean your mind stream.

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:15.187
It doesn't mean logic
or clear thinking that's

00:03:15.187 --> 00:03:16.936
RIGS PA

00:03:16.936 --> 00:03:19.997
RIG PA'I YA MTHA' THUG MED DU BSGRUB DGOS

00:03:19.997 --> 00:03:20.830
You must prove

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:21.730
BSGRUB PA

00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:24.983
DGOS means you must prove
that your mind has had

00:03:24.983 --> 00:03:26.500
no beginning.

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:28.805
You cannot point to a beginning.

00:03:28.805 --> 00:03:33.204
YA MTHA' THUG MED means

00:03:33.204 --> 00:03:35.840
'THUG MED means that you never will hit

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:38.173
a beginning point.

00:03:38.173 --> 00:03:42.620
YA MTHA' means if you go looking for

00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:44.700
the first moment of awareness,

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:47.510
the first moment of Michael's
awareness in history,

00:03:47.510 --> 00:03:49.430
you will never find it.

00:03:49.430 --> 00:03:53.050
Look at this lady's face.

00:03:53.050 --> 00:03:57.230
It's something we're
supposed to think about.

00:03:57.230 --> 00:04:00.110
It's difficult. It's just hard.

00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:04.260
What I've learned in a long life is that

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:09.260
when things are hard to
understand, then you have to stop

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:14.390
and you have to try to
understand. You have to stop.

00:04:14.390 --> 00:04:18.240
I study scriptures a lot

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:21.510
and I worked very, very
hard on them. I just,

00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:24.350
over many years time, I got into a habit

00:04:24.350 --> 00:04:27.530
that my teacher taught
me, and you just stop.

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:29.760
You figure it out. You don't skip it.

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:31.470
And you don't go ahead and

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:33.943
if it takes you three
days to figure it out,

00:04:33.943 --> 00:04:37.428
then you spend three days on
it because it's important.

00:04:37.428 --> 00:04:41.570
DE RING GI SEMS 'DI KHA SANG
GI SEMS KYI RGYUN YIN ZHING

00:04:41.570 --> 00:04:45.112
DE RING GI SEMS means your mind of today.

00:04:45.112 --> 00:04:49.023
KHA SANG GI SEMS means
your mind of yesterday.

00:04:49.023 --> 00:04:52.130
RGYUN means is the flow.

00:04:52.130 --> 00:04:57.130
Your present thoughts are
the flow or the stream

00:04:57.710 --> 00:05:00.475
of yesterday's thoughts continuing.

00:05:00.475 --> 00:05:03.720
DE'ANG KHA NYIN GYI RIG
RGYUN YIN PA NAS BZUNG

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:08.603
And yesterday's thoughts are KHA NYIN.

00:05:08.603 --> 00:05:11.310
KHA NYIN means KHES NYIN
PA in colloquial Tibetan,

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:13.150
means the day before yesterday.

00:05:13.150 --> 00:05:18.070
So yesterday's thoughts are
the continuation of the flow

00:05:18.070 --> 00:05:20.366
of the thoughts of the day before.

00:05:20.366 --> 00:05:24.160
YIN PA NAS BZUNG means
and you can track it back,

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:25.915
you can track it back.

00:05:25.915 --> 00:05:28.980
MA'I MNGAL NAS SKYES MA THAG PA'I SEMS

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:32.410
You can go back to the
state of mind you had

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:35.555
just after you came out
of your mother's womb.

00:05:35.555 --> 00:05:37.490
MNGAL NAS SKYES

00:05:37.490 --> 00:05:41.480
Don't forget, in Buddhism there's
two kinds of birth, SKYES.

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:44.260
One is MNGAL NAS SKYES, which is here,

00:05:44.260 --> 00:05:46.830
when you actually come
out of your mother's womb,

00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:51.470
but technically in Buddhism,
the moment of conception

00:05:51.470 --> 00:05:54.947
is the beginning of this
birth, of this rebirth.

00:05:54.947 --> 00:05:56.830
SKYES MA THAG PA'I SEMS

00:05:56.830 --> 00:06:01.830
So if you go back to the
state of mind you had

00:06:02.290 --> 00:06:06.016
on the day that you came out
of your mom in the hospital,

00:06:06.016 --> 00:06:09.420
SKYE KHA MA'I RGYUN YIN ZHING

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:11.840
that's the,

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:15.587
what your mind today can be traced back

00:06:15.587 --> 00:06:17.316
to the state of mind you had.

00:06:17.316 --> 00:06:20.870
SKYE KHA MA means just
after you were born,

00:06:20.870 --> 00:06:23.661
at the moment of birth. But

00:06:23.661 --> 00:06:26.470
MNGAL DU ZHUGS MA THAG PA'I SEMS DE

00:06:26.470 --> 00:06:29.703
but you can also track that
back to the mind you had.

00:06:29.703 --> 00:06:32.346
This ZHUGS is the past tense of 'JUG

00:06:32.346 --> 00:06:35.610
which means when you
entered your mom's womb.

00:06:35.610 --> 00:06:39.200
So the state of mind that you had

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:42.350
on the day you came out of
your mom in the hospital

00:06:42.350 --> 00:06:45.570
is really the continuation of the flow

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:48.395
of the mind which entered
your mother's womb,

00:06:48.395 --> 00:06:51.019
nine months and 10 days before.

00:06:51.019 --> 00:06:53.577
MNGAL MA THAG PA'I SEMS DE ZHUGS KHA MA'I

00:06:53.577 --> 00:06:56.410
RIG PA'I RGYUN YIN PA'I PHYIR

00:06:56.410 --> 00:07:01.330
So you can trace your mind back to...

00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:05.470
All scientists would agree,
all westerners would agree

00:07:05.470 --> 00:07:09.700
that you can trace your
stream of mind back to

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:12.590
the moment after you entered the womb.

00:07:12.590 --> 00:07:16.550
Now, if you existed before
that, that's a debate,

00:07:16.550 --> 00:07:21.080
but nobody would say you
cannot trace this consciousness

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:24.540
back to the womb.

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:27.665
'KHOR BA LA THOG MA'I MTHA' MED PAS

00:07:27.665 --> 00:07:31.297
SEMS KYI 'GO BRTZOM PA 'DI'O, ,ZHES PA

00:07:31.297 --> 00:07:33.438
'KHOR BA LA THOG MA'I MTHA' MED PA means

00:07:33.438 --> 00:07:35.171
THOG MA means beginning.

00:07:35.171 --> 00:07:37.780
MTHA' means front-end.

00:07:37.780 --> 00:07:42.780
So the front-end of your
lives, of your rebirth,

00:07:42.946 --> 00:07:43.788
MTHA' MED

00:07:43.788 --> 00:07:48.780
you can't point to a certain
point at which you started,

00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:52.750
where your lifetimes
in this circle started.

00:07:52.750 --> 00:07:57.750
The name for this life is
sansara, which means a circle.

00:07:59.130 --> 00:08:02.480
It means that, as soon
as you finish one life,

00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:03.980
you picking up on another life,

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:05.600
and then you pick up on another life,

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:07.063
and then it's a circle.

00:08:07.063 --> 00:08:09.079
'GO BRTZOM PA 'DI'O,

00:08:09.079 --> 00:08:12.854
This 'GO is spelled 'a-o ga naro' 'GO

00:08:12.854 --> 00:08:15.071
which doesn't mean head.

00:08:15.071 --> 00:08:20.071
If it's 'ma-o ga naro'
MGO, M-G-O, it means head.

00:08:20.313 --> 00:08:22.530
This 'GO means to begin.

00:08:22.530 --> 00:08:27.530
So 'GO BRTZOM PA means you
cannot point to a certain point

00:08:27.620 --> 00:08:30.440
in time, in history, and say

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:33.272
that was the beginning of my mind.

00:08:33.272 --> 00:08:35.531
ZHIG GANG DU'ANG MI RNYED PAS

00:08:35.531 --> 00:08:37.950
You won't be able to find it.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:41.690
By the way, this find is
the same verb that we use

00:08:41.690 --> 00:08:44.170
when you go looking for an object

00:08:44.170 --> 00:08:46.360
which is not coming from you.

00:08:46.360 --> 00:08:49.490
When you talk about two
husbands in a kitchen

00:08:49.490 --> 00:08:53.070
and you try to find a husband
that's not coming from you,

00:08:53.070 --> 00:08:55.070
that's called RNYED, same verb.

00:08:55.070 --> 00:08:59.410
You can attempt to
locate, it's called RNYED.

00:08:59.410 --> 00:09:01.997
You can go looking for a husband
who's not coming from you,

00:09:01.997 --> 00:09:03.880
but you won't find it.

00:09:03.880 --> 00:09:07.270
You can go looking for a first
moment of your awareness,

00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:09.961
of your consciousness,
but you won't find it.

00:09:09.961 --> 00:09:13.520
RANG GI SKYE BA LA'ANG THOG MA'I MTHA' MED

00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:18.170
Therefore, because
there's no beginning point

00:09:18.170 --> 00:09:21.440
of the river of your mind,

00:09:21.440 --> 00:09:25.610
therefore, there's no first
birth that you ever had.

00:09:25.610 --> 00:09:30.610
Because if there's no
beginning point of the river

00:09:31.390 --> 00:09:33.130
or the flow of your mind,

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:35.903
then there's no first birth either.

00:09:35.903 --> 00:09:38.780
MTHA' MED PAR GRUB LA

00:09:38.780 --> 00:09:40.170
And this is an old argument

00:09:40.170 --> 00:09:43.903
which I've described to
you many times, but...

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:51.770
I was brought up in school,
when I was taught in school,

00:09:51.770 --> 00:09:55.490
we were taught that things
should have a beginning

00:09:55.490 --> 00:09:58.600
ཊhen they teach us the Big Bang

00:09:58.600 --> 00:10:01.260
But if you think careful about it,

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:03.690
the idea of a first beginning,

00:10:03.690 --> 00:10:06.610
is illogical. It's not logical.

00:10:06.610 --> 00:10:11.020
It's comfortable to us
because we grew up with it.

00:10:11.020 --> 00:10:13.700
Oftentimes when you teach people

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:16.600
that sansara has no beginning,

00:10:16.600 --> 00:10:18.910
it feels uncomfortable to them

00:10:18.910 --> 00:10:21.470
if they learned something else in school,

00:10:21.470 --> 00:10:23.980
when they're a kid. But if you say,

00:10:23.980 --> 00:10:26.700
look, you're not a kid
anymore, now you're grown up,

00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:28.810
now you have to think for yourself.

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:33.810
Does it make sense that
everything has a cause,

00:10:33.830 --> 00:10:36.597
except the first thing of everything?

00:10:36.597 --> 00:10:38.764
That doesn't make sense, come on.

00:10:38.764 --> 00:10:43.260
Then once you grow up, you
have to give up this idea

00:10:43.260 --> 00:10:47.270
that a beginning is more logical

00:10:47.270 --> 00:10:50.650
because it's not more
logical, it's illogical.

00:10:50.650 --> 00:10:52.320
It's illogical

00:10:52.320 --> 00:10:56.110
that something which goes
on in a flow for 68 years

00:10:56.110 --> 00:11:00.900
should have a beginning
where it didn't have a flow.

00:11:00.900 --> 00:11:03.113
That doesn't make sense.

00:11:03.113 --> 00:11:04.802
THOG MA'I MTHA' MED PAR GRUB LA

00:11:04.802 --> 00:11:05.950
You can prove

00:11:05.950 --> 00:11:08.746
that there's no beginning
to the flow of your mind.

00:11:08.746 --> 00:11:11.505
DE GRUB PAS SKYE BA GRANGS KYIS MI CHOD PA

00:11:11.505 --> 00:11:13.022
ZHIG YOD PAR GRUB PAS

00:11:13.022 --> 00:11:18.020
If you prove that the flow
or the river of your thoughts

00:11:18.020 --> 00:11:21.040
or your awareness never had a beginning,

00:11:21.040 --> 00:11:24.120
then by implication,

00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:26.870
you prove that you have
never had a first birth.

00:11:26.870 --> 00:11:29.355
You have never had a first rebirth.

00:11:29.355 --> 00:11:30.988
GRUB PAS SKYE BA LA YA MTHA' MED

00:11:30.988 --> 00:11:34.490
Therefore, there is no beginning point

00:11:34.490 --> 00:11:36.990
to the process of you being born.

00:11:36.990 --> 00:11:39.550
Die, born, die, born,
die, born, die, born.

00:11:39.550 --> 00:11:41.343
There's no beginning to that.

00:11:41.343 --> 00:11:45.160
All right, I like this image.

00:11:45.160 --> 00:11:46.660
I was trying to...

00:11:46.660 --> 00:11:48.120
My job, part of my job,

00:11:48.120 --> 00:11:52.280
when I prepare for a Lam Rim
teaching is to find pictures

00:11:53.470 --> 00:11:57.210
or images that can help
you remember the ideas.

00:11:57.210 --> 00:11:59.930
Again, these are IDIMS, idea images and

00:11:59.930 --> 00:12:04.810
it's good for you.
Traditionally in the Lam Rim

00:12:04.810 --> 00:12:08.740
you're supposed to review three times.

00:12:08.740 --> 00:12:11.840
Right after you get home,
after you'd listened to this,

00:12:11.840 --> 00:12:14.850
you're supposed to close your
eyes and review everything.

00:12:14.850 --> 00:12:18.190
Then that evening, you're
supposed to review again.

00:12:18.190 --> 00:12:19.420
And then the next morning,

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:21.980
you're supposed to review again.

00:12:21.980 --> 00:12:26.980
I'm trying to find photographs or images

00:12:27.340 --> 00:12:29.810
that will help you review.

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:33.070
So an easy way to review the Lam Rim,

00:12:33.070 --> 00:12:35.770
what you're supposed
to do if you want it to

00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:37.370
affect your mind.

00:12:37.370 --> 00:12:38.530
A great thing to do

00:12:38.530 --> 00:12:41.402
is to go through the pictures
that I'm showing you.

00:12:41.402 --> 00:12:44.460
When you finish the class,

00:12:44.460 --> 00:12:47.100
right after you finish the
class, go through the pictures.

00:12:47.100 --> 00:12:50.290
Do you remember what
that picture represents?

00:12:50.290 --> 00:12:52.710
Pao, what's the picture of the lady

00:12:52.710 --> 00:12:54.820
going like this represent?

00:12:54.820 --> 00:12:56.950
Or Gyelse? Venerable Gyelse.

00:12:56.950 --> 00:12:59.559
Why is she? That was
the first picture today.

00:12:59.559 --> 00:13:01.568
[Student] Thinking about past life.

00:13:01.568 --> 00:13:03.710
Yeah, she's trying to figure it out.

00:13:03.710 --> 00:13:07.090
Did I have a past life or
didn't I have a past life?

00:13:07.090 --> 00:13:10.210
Don't say you figured it out easily

00:13:10.210 --> 00:13:14.120
because if you did, you didn't.

00:13:14.120 --> 00:13:17.620
It's difficult. It's
really, really, really hard.

00:13:17.620 --> 00:13:20.450
So when you see that picture I
want you to think about that.

00:13:20.450 --> 00:13:22.620
Now, the picture I'm talking about now,

00:13:22.620 --> 00:13:25.869
is this, I don't know,
it's an ocean or something,

00:13:25.869 --> 00:13:28.353
with an ouroboros.

00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:32.950
I don't know how to
pronounce it, ouroboros.

00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:35.100
Yeah, I like these two images.

00:13:35.100 --> 00:13:37.760
I put these two images together.

00:13:37.760 --> 00:13:42.240
That a snake eating its tail is called,

00:13:42.240 --> 00:13:45.498
I don't know how to
pronounce it, ouroboros?

00:13:46.981 --> 00:13:50.800
It represents

00:13:50.800 --> 00:13:53.580
a cycle that continues upon itself.

00:13:53.580 --> 00:13:55.562
A circle which,

00:13:55.562 --> 00:13:57.990
an ending which becomes a beginning.

00:13:57.990 --> 00:14:00.190
Can you keep the image up?
I'm going to talk about it.

00:14:00.190 --> 00:14:01.840
Yeah, good, thank you Pachi.

00:14:01.840 --> 00:14:06.210
So I'm thinking of the water in the lake:

00:14:06.210 --> 00:14:10.420
how it sits in the lake,

00:14:10.420 --> 00:14:15.420
then it evaporates,
then it becomes a cloud,

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:17.390
then the cloud runs around,

00:14:17.390 --> 00:14:19.590
then the cloud turns into rain,

00:14:19.590 --> 00:14:22.480
the rain falls in the
lake, and it's a cycle

00:14:22.480 --> 00:14:25.260
similar to the snake
that's eating its tail.

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:29.500
By the way, I like
languages and I looked up,

00:14:29.500 --> 00:14:32.938
what's the root of ouroboros.

00:14:32.938 --> 00:14:35.664
[Student] Ouroboros.
Ouroboros, okay.

00:14:35.664 --> 00:14:38.339
And it's very interesting.

00:14:40.870 --> 00:14:43.900
'Boros' means to eat.

00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:48.900
It's got a lot of roots in Russian.

00:14:49.383 --> 00:14:53.290
'бороться' means fight with a sword.

00:14:53.290 --> 00:14:55.794
And Boris comes from that

00:14:55.794 --> 00:15:00.721
because it's a sword fighter.

00:15:00.721 --> 00:15:03.810
So 'бороться' means to fight

00:15:03.810 --> 00:15:06.740
with swords and chop up things.

00:15:06.740 --> 00:15:11.740
'Ouru' comes from 'ors' which became arse,

00:15:11.820 --> 00:15:13.830
which means your ass.

00:15:13.830 --> 00:15:15.400
I thought it was so cute.

00:15:15.400 --> 00:15:19.340
So arse eater, arse chopper.

00:15:19.340 --> 00:15:21.740
Arse chopper with your teeth

00:15:21.740 --> 00:15:25.350
means the snake that eats its own tail.

00:15:25.350 --> 00:15:27.950
I think it's a nice image,

00:15:27.950 --> 00:15:30.480
a nice Irish image for

00:15:31.710 --> 00:15:34.290
things that perpetuate themselves.

00:15:34.290 --> 00:15:37.270
Self-perpetuating cycles.

00:15:37.270 --> 00:15:40.360
I think it's a perfect
picture in the way that

00:15:40.360 --> 00:15:44.280
rain becomes lakes, lakes become clouds

00:15:44.280 --> 00:15:46.897
and clouds become rain.

00:15:46.897 --> 00:15:49.568
DAS NA TSE 'DI'I AA MA YOD PA BZHIN DU

00:15:49.568 --> 00:15:52.967
TSE SNGA MA'I MNGAL SKYES
DANG SGONG SKYE GNYIS

00:15:52.967 --> 00:15:53.800
DES NA

00:15:53.800 --> 00:15:55.425
Therefore,

00:15:55.425 --> 00:15:57.162
TSE 'DI'I AA MA

00:15:57.162 --> 00:15:58.187
There's a joke.

00:15:58.187 --> 00:16:00.786
When I was trying to get
into a Tibetan class,

00:16:00.786 --> 00:16:02.970
when I first started Tibetan.

00:16:02.970 --> 00:16:04.770
The teacher wanted me to be in the class,

00:16:04.770 --> 00:16:08.900
but there was this
administrator to the college

00:16:08.900 --> 00:16:12.570
that didn't want me to be in the class.

00:16:12.570 --> 00:16:16.120
They agreed that they would test me

00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:19.790
with some Tibetan words to see
if I could get in the class.

00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:23.420
So I went into the test.
I was really nervous

00:16:23.420 --> 00:16:25.060
because I knew like five words.

00:16:25.060 --> 00:16:29.430
And the guy who wanted
me in the class, he said,

00:16:29.430 --> 00:16:33.680
"Okay, what is AA MA and AA PHA mean?

00:16:33.680 --> 00:16:36.230
I said, "Mom and Dad?"

00:16:36.230 --> 00:16:39.292
He said, "Correct, you're in the class."

00:16:39.292 --> 00:16:41.279
The other guy was really irritated.

00:16:41.279 --> 00:16:44.879
DES NA AA MA YOD PA BZHIN DU means

00:16:44.879 --> 00:16:49.313
you had an AA MA, you
had a mom in this life.

00:16:49.313 --> 00:16:52.396
BZHIN DU TSE SNGA MA'I
MNGAL SKYE DANG SGONG SKYES

00:16:52.396 --> 00:16:53.494
Now he says,

00:16:53.494 --> 00:16:57.843
$50 question for the advanced
students in the room.

00:16:58.930 --> 00:17:03.930
He says, with reference
to birth from a womb

00:17:04.140 --> 00:17:07.430
and to birth from an egg.

00:17:07.430 --> 00:17:09.510
Why does he say that?

00:17:09.510 --> 00:17:14.355
With reference to birth from
the womb and birth from an egg.

00:17:14.355 --> 00:17:17.665
[Student] You can say the
two did come from a mother.

00:17:17.665 --> 00:17:20.340
Yeah, good, yeah!

00:17:20.340 --> 00:17:22.532
How many kinds of births
are there in total?

00:17:22.532 --> 00:17:23.647
Four.

00:17:25.300 --> 00:17:27.990
According to Buddhism and by the way,

00:17:27.990 --> 00:17:30.320
this is one of the first
teachings of the Buddha.

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:32.910
It's considered a big part

00:17:32.910 --> 00:17:34.960
of the first turning of the wheel,

00:17:34.960 --> 00:17:39.960
that there's four ways to take
birth. What's the other two?

00:17:40.420 --> 00:17:43.940
DROD GSHER LAS SKYE BA which means,

00:17:43.940 --> 00:17:47.940
when mosquitoes are
born from warm water and

00:17:47.940 --> 00:17:51.120
warm water -- DROD GSHER

00:17:51.120 --> 00:17:52.590
because they didn't know
they were eggs in there,

00:17:52.590 --> 00:17:54.400
and they were too small to see.

00:17:54.400 --> 00:17:56.807
What's the other one?

00:17:56.807 --> 00:17:57.949
RDZUS TE SKYE

00:17:57.949 --> 00:17:59.880
Where you born in a lotus

00:17:59.880 --> 00:18:04.200
or like Patanjali, he's
born in his mother's hands.

00:18:04.200 --> 00:18:09.200
It's interesting that
Pabongka is a great debater,

00:18:09.950 --> 00:18:12.190
although he was a very gentle person

00:18:12.190 --> 00:18:13.790
and a very kind teacher,

00:18:13.790 --> 00:18:17.070
he wasn't this kind of
arrogant debater type.

00:18:17.070 --> 00:18:21.098
But he's covering his ass.

00:18:21.098 --> 00:18:24.173
By the way with reference
to two kinds of birth.

00:18:24.173 --> 00:18:26.348
SKABS KYI AA MA RE DGOS PAS

00:18:26.348 --> 00:18:28.100
You got to have AA MA RE.

00:18:28.100 --> 00:18:30.900
RE RE means each.

00:18:30.900 --> 00:18:35.040
For each birth there has to be a mom.

00:18:35.040 --> 00:18:38.660
Each birth has to have
a corresponding mother.

00:18:38.660 --> 00:18:40.880
So the RE is very important here.

00:18:40.880 --> 00:18:41.713
DGOS PAS

00:18:41.713 --> 00:18:42.804
You got to have

00:18:42.804 --> 00:18:44.988
DE 'DRA'I SKYE BA GCIG LEN PA LA

00:18:44.988 --> 00:18:48.540
Therefore, if you have one birth,

00:18:48.540 --> 00:18:50.930
which is one of those two kinds

00:18:50.930 --> 00:18:53.840
from the womb or from the eggs,

00:18:53.840 --> 00:18:56.213
you got to have one mom each.

00:18:56.213 --> 00:18:58.070
AA MA GCIC DGOS PA BZHIN DU

00:18:58.070 --> 00:19:01.883
By the way, in a debate, if you agree,

00:19:03.270 --> 00:19:07.170
it's like a chess game. The
guy's going to set you up.

00:19:07.170 --> 00:19:10.160
In the beginning he'll look very innocent.

00:19:10.160 --> 00:19:11.960
He'll move a pawn

00:19:11.960 --> 00:19:16.420
and then suddenly you realize
he trapped you already.

00:19:16.420 --> 00:19:19.950
With the first two moves or three moves.

00:19:19.950 --> 00:19:23.240
In a debate you're like, "Okay,

00:19:23.240 --> 00:19:27.380
if you're born from a womb,
each birth needs a mom, right?"

00:19:27.380 --> 00:19:29.900
And so, just one each, right?

00:19:29.900 --> 00:19:34.630
Then you're already
committed to countless moms.

00:19:34.630 --> 00:19:36.380
Just one each, right?

00:19:36.380 --> 00:19:39.144
One each, I don't have
a problem with that.

00:19:39.144 --> 00:19:40.898
SKYE BA BRGYA LEN PA NA

00:19:40.898 --> 00:19:42.660
If you take a 100 births,

00:19:42.660 --> 00:19:46.035
then you got to have MA
BRGYA. What's that mean?

00:19:46.035 --> 00:19:48.490
You got to have 100 mothers,
100 births, 100 mothers.

00:19:48.490 --> 00:19:50.823
Hey, you agreed, one-to-one.

00:19:52.669 --> 00:19:55.891
STONG LEN PA NA MA STONG

00:19:55.891 --> 00:19:57.915
If you take a 1000 rebirths,

00:19:57.915 --> 00:19:59.835
then you got a thousand moms.

00:19:59.835 --> 00:20:02.785
Therefore, GRANGS MED DGOS

00:20:04.420 --> 00:20:09.420
It must be, you know
this GRANGS from Sankhya,

00:20:10.450 --> 00:20:12.650
GRANGS CAN BA

00:20:12.650 --> 00:20:15.352
The count must be, it must be countless.

00:20:15.352 --> 00:20:19.010
SEMS CAN THAMS CAD KYIS
MA MA BYAS PA'I THABS MED

00:20:19.010 --> 00:20:22.775
Double negative, the first MA is mom.

00:20:22.775 --> 00:20:27.032
Now there's two negatives,
what's that mean?

00:20:27.032 --> 00:20:31.002
MA MA BYAS PA'I THABS MED, MA MA MED

00:20:32.081 --> 00:20:35.490
MA MA MED

00:20:35.490 --> 00:20:40.163
There's nobody who hasn't been your mom.

00:20:40.163 --> 00:20:42.360
MA MA BYAS PA'I THABS MED

00:20:42.360 --> 00:20:46.980
There's no way anyone
has not been your mom.

00:20:46.980 --> 00:20:50.520
You agreed one-to-one: one birth one mom.

00:20:50.520 --> 00:20:52.870
Countless births, countless moms.

00:20:52.870 --> 00:20:55.560
Therefore, everyone's been your mom.

00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:58.970
I like this picture. I call
it, It's just the odds.

00:20:58.970 --> 00:21:00.830
I found this photo, I like it.

00:21:00.830 --> 00:21:03.580
It's the numbers coming
out of this guy's hands.

00:21:03.580 --> 00:21:07.340
And it's just math.

00:21:07.340 --> 00:21:09.640
Do you agree that to have one--

00:21:09.640 --> 00:21:12.470
Do you agree that to be born
once you have to have a mom?

00:21:12.470 --> 00:21:15.480
Yes, I agree. Then, you
agree to countless moms.

00:21:15.480 --> 00:21:17.322
Everyone's been your mother.

00:21:17.322 --> 00:21:22.322
It's just mathematics. It's
not Buddhism. It's math.

00:21:22.674 --> 00:21:27.107
DE LA 'DI LTAR, AA MA MANG DU DGOS MOD,

00:21:27.107 --> 00:21:29.832
SEMS CAN NI MTHA' YAS PAS DE THAMS CAD NI

00:21:29.832 --> 00:21:32.160
AA MA CANG MIN NO ZHE NA

00:21:32.160 --> 00:21:36.940
Now, Pabongka starts to
present the natural objections

00:21:36.940 --> 00:21:39.970
that come up in your mind to these ideas.

00:21:39.970 --> 00:21:41.777
The minute I say,

00:21:41.777 --> 00:21:44.850
is there one mom required for each birth?

00:21:44.850 --> 00:21:47.450
- Yes. - Have you had countless births?

00:21:47.450 --> 00:21:50.597
- Yes. - Well then, do
you have countless moms?

00:21:50.597 --> 00:21:51.980
- No.

00:21:51.980 --> 00:21:54.986
Then you say, What? But you have to.

00:21:54.986 --> 00:21:56.820
And you say, no, no.

00:21:56.820 --> 00:22:00.620
Geshe-la, the Buddhism says many times

00:22:00.620 --> 00:22:02.480
that living beings are countless.

00:22:02.480 --> 00:22:04.290
Living beings are countless.

00:22:04.290 --> 00:22:08.010
I understand one-on-one, I understand, but

00:22:08.010 --> 00:22:11.980
how many for countless?
Living beings are countless.

00:22:11.980 --> 00:22:14.230
How can everyone be my mom?

00:22:15.673 --> 00:22:20.073
SPYIR RANG GI SKYE BA MANG
BAR MA ZAD KYI; BYE BRAG

00:22:20.073 --> 00:22:21.860
And then he gets--

00:22:21.860 --> 00:22:25.170
Instead of answering the question,

00:22:25.170 --> 00:22:29.810
he kills the guy with more information.

00:22:29.810 --> 00:22:34.610
He goes deeper. He says,
"Look, forget your question.

00:22:34.610 --> 00:22:37.505
Let's talk about the
different kinds of beings."

00:22:37.505 --> 00:22:39.810
SPYIR RANG GI SKYE BA MANG BAR MA ZAD

00:22:39.810 --> 00:22:42.370
You've had lots of moms, you want to say

00:22:42.370 --> 00:22:46.000
not countless, I don't
care, that's all right.

00:22:46.000 --> 00:22:49.520
But, BYE BRAG, okay? Here's SPYI BYE BRAG.

00:22:49.520 --> 00:22:53.070
At the beginning of the
sentence is SPYI with a R,

00:22:53.070 --> 00:22:54.078
and then BYE BRAG.

00:22:54.078 --> 00:22:56.040
SPYIR means generally speaking,

00:22:56.040 --> 00:23:00.290
you had lots of moms.
But more particularly,

00:23:00.290 --> 00:23:02.040
let's talk about wild animals.

00:23:02.040 --> 00:23:05.430
RI DVAGS means wild animals.

00:23:05.430 --> 00:23:09.170
Animals of the wild, of the wilderness.

00:23:09.170 --> 00:23:13.320
For example, SHA BA means a deer,

00:23:13.320 --> 00:23:15.730
and DGO BA means an antelope.

00:23:15.730 --> 00:23:20.730
'BU SRIN means bugs, insects, ants,

00:23:21.720 --> 00:23:24.232
grasshoppers, 'BU SRIN

00:23:24.232 --> 00:23:26.982
SOGS RE RE NAS KYI LUS
BLANGS PA'ANG GRANGS MED CING

00:23:26.982 --> 00:23:30.730
The number of times you have put on

00:23:30.730 --> 00:23:33.430
a grasshopper body are countless.

00:23:33.430 --> 00:23:36.879
How do you say grasshopper
in Spanish? I'm curious.

00:23:36.879 --> 00:23:38.996
[Student] Saltamontes.

00:23:38.996 --> 00:23:40.921
[Student] Saltamontes.

00:23:40.921 --> 00:23:44.490
Saltamontes? Oh cool.

00:23:44.490 --> 00:23:46.062
What's salta?

00:23:46.062 --> 00:23:46.895
[Student] Jump.

00:23:46.895 --> 00:23:49.708
Jump, mountain jumper?

00:23:49.708 --> 00:23:52.831
Saltamontes, okay cool.

00:23:52.831 --> 00:23:55.694
Saltamontes, so you
have been a saltamontes.

00:23:55.694 --> 00:23:57.448
LUS BLANGS PA'ANG GRANGS MED

00:23:57.448 --> 00:24:02.180
The times you have been just a
grasshopper, not other being,

00:24:02.180 --> 00:24:04.840
just a grasshopper, is also countless.

00:24:04.840 --> 00:24:06.858
Forget the human rebirth.

00:24:06.858 --> 00:24:08.110
The times you have been a

00:24:08.110 --> 00:24:10.363
grasshopper has been
countless, saltamontes.

00:24:10.363 --> 00:24:12.430
DE LTAR SEMS CAN GYI RIGS GRANGS MED PA

00:24:12.430 --> 00:24:16.230
The different types of
beings are countless.

00:24:16.230 --> 00:24:21.187
The different species of beings
are countless. Therefore,

00:24:21.187 --> 00:24:23.318
SEMS CAN GYI RIGS GRANGS
MED PA RE RE'I 'ANG

00:24:23.318 --> 00:24:25.880
among those countless species

00:24:25.880 --> 00:24:28.110
you have taken countless births

00:24:28.110 --> 00:24:30.460
in each one of the countless species.

00:24:30.460 --> 00:24:31.293
So how many births is that, please?

00:24:31.293 --> 00:24:34.609
Countless times countless.

00:24:36.348 --> 00:24:40.656
GRANGS MED PA BLANGS PA'I
PHYIR, SEMS CAN LAS KYANG

00:24:40.656 --> 00:24:42.510
GRANGS MANG BA'I SKYE BA BLANGS LA

00:24:42.510 --> 00:24:46.180
Therefore, you have taken more births

00:24:46.180 --> 00:24:49.823
than the number of living
beings in the universe.

00:24:51.620 --> 00:24:55.380
Because they're just stuck
in one form of life now,

00:24:55.380 --> 00:24:58.940
but you have to multiply
that times countless.

00:24:58.940 --> 00:25:00.110
Don't tell me,

00:25:00.110 --> 00:25:02.640
Geshe-la, there's countless
beings in the universe.

00:25:02.640 --> 00:25:05.160
I agree. But don't forget

00:25:05.160 --> 00:25:08.804
each countless being
had countless rebirths

00:25:08.804 --> 00:25:11.450
as this grasshopper.

00:25:11.450 --> 00:25:13.960
That's countless times
countless times countless.

00:25:13.960 --> 00:25:17.485
Don't tell me they haven't been your mom.

00:25:17.485 --> 00:25:19.870
Okay, it's kind of cool.

00:25:22.550 --> 00:25:25.920
DE'I TSE NA AA MA'ANG
GRANGS DE MTSUNGS DGOS PAS

00:25:25.920 --> 00:25:30.500
Each time you were born as a grasshopper,

00:25:30.500 --> 00:25:32.690
we got a bug here, we've got a worm here.

00:25:32.690 --> 00:25:35.910
You got a picture of a worm?

00:25:35.910 --> 00:25:37.401
I think so.

00:25:40.450 --> 00:25:43.790
I'm thinking about worms
because it's springtime.

00:25:43.790 --> 00:25:47.890
I'm working in my garden. I'm
trying not to hurt the worms.

00:25:47.890 --> 00:25:50.740
They say they survive if you cut them.

00:25:50.740 --> 00:25:53.380
Each half survives and becomes a worm.

00:25:53.380 --> 00:25:55.360
But I just keep thinking about,

00:25:55.360 --> 00:25:56.970
would I like to be cut in half?

00:25:56.970 --> 00:26:01.500
Then I say, no. So I try to
avoid, I try to help them.

00:26:01.500 --> 00:26:03.600
And then,

00:26:03.600 --> 00:26:08.340
you've had countless
rebirths just as a worm.

00:26:08.340 --> 00:26:10.803
You've had countless
rebirths just as a worm.

00:26:10.803 --> 00:26:15.240
SEMS CAN THAMS CAD KYIS
AA MA BYAS PA TZAM MA ZAD

00:26:15.240 --> 00:26:19.030
Not only has every living
being been your mother

00:26:19.030 --> 00:26:21.750
but they have been your
mother countless times

00:26:21.750 --> 00:26:25.510
in each of the countless forms of life.

00:26:25.510 --> 00:26:30.000
Everybody has been your mother as a worm,

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:31.690
countless times.

00:26:31.690 --> 00:26:33.270
And then multiply that times

00:26:33.270 --> 00:26:35.620
how many different life forms are there.

00:26:35.620 --> 00:26:38.613
That's how many moms you've had.

00:26:38.613 --> 00:26:40.410
YIN NO

00:26:40.410 --> 00:26:45.100
Then he quotes a very
beautiful book by Nagarjuna.

00:26:45.100 --> 00:26:46.652
It's one of the two books

00:26:46.652 --> 00:26:49.293
I'm thinking to give a friend of mine,

00:26:50.590 --> 00:26:53.450
because it's a extremely valuable book

00:26:55.000 --> 00:26:59.860
and it's probably the first
Lam Rim, which is BSHES SPRING

00:26:59.860 --> 00:27:02.720
Letter to a Friend, Suhṛllekha.

00:27:02.720 --> 00:27:05.710
Which is really suhṛd lekha

00:27:05.710 --> 00:27:07.770
and the D changes to L.

00:27:07.770 --> 00:27:10.680
suhṛd means good heart,

00:27:10.680 --> 00:27:14.250
and lekha means an epistle,

00:27:14.250 --> 00:27:16.082
which comes from rekhā,

00:27:16.082 --> 00:27:18.774
which means to scratch something.

00:27:18.774 --> 00:27:22.700
Anyway, BSHES SPRING
means Letter to a Friend.

00:27:22.700 --> 00:27:25.520
And Nagarjuna wrote a letter to

00:27:25.520 --> 00:27:29.390
a king named Udayabhadra,
if I'm not mistaken.

00:27:29.390 --> 00:27:32.993
That would be a great text to translate.

00:27:34.241 --> 00:27:39.241
MA YI THUG MTHA' RGYA SHUG TSI GU TZAM

00:27:39.634 --> 00:27:41.362
MA YI THUG MTHA'

00:27:41.362 --> 00:27:45.970
means establishing the ultimate
number of moms you've had,

00:27:45.970 --> 00:27:49.323
could be illustrated by RGYA SHUG TSI GU.

00:27:49.323 --> 00:27:54.170
RGYA SHUG means a juniper
tree and we have them,

00:27:54.170 --> 00:27:56.340
tens of thousands around here.

00:27:56.340 --> 00:28:00.570
Which I like, I like them, I
think they're beautiful and

00:28:00.570 --> 00:28:03.343
they give everybody allergies.

00:28:05.293 --> 00:28:10.293
TSI GU means a small ball that you make,

00:28:10.650 --> 00:28:12.440
like a small ball of,

00:28:13.940 --> 00:28:16.560
like if you take some mud
and you make a tiny ball

00:28:16.560 --> 00:28:19.280
out of it. That's called a TSI GU.

00:28:19.280 --> 00:28:24.280
ZHES SOGS KYI DNGOS BSTAN MA'I MA,

00:28:25.088 --> 00:28:26.810
DE'I MA SOGS LA SBYAR YANG

00:28:26.810 --> 00:28:30.400
Let's apply that statement from Nagarjuna

00:28:30.400 --> 00:28:35.030
and that statement by
Nagarjuna is, if you sit

00:28:35.030 --> 00:28:37.907
and you make,

00:28:38.950 --> 00:28:43.110
if you sit on the ground
like a kid on a rainy day

00:28:43.110 --> 00:28:46.260
and you make little balls of mud,

00:28:46.260 --> 00:28:48.373
the size of a juniper berry,

00:28:49.990 --> 00:28:53.657
how long would it take
to run out of planet?

00:28:56.820 --> 00:28:59.620
How long would it take
to run out of the planet?

00:29:00.670 --> 00:29:05.670
Pabongka Rinpoche says,
there's a tradition

00:29:06.060 --> 00:29:09.610
that you don't count it the way it sounds.

00:29:09.610 --> 00:29:13.223
You don't say this is my mom.

00:29:14.840 --> 00:29:17.910
This person was my mom.
This person was my mom.

00:29:17.910 --> 00:29:19.375
This person was my mom.

00:29:19.375 --> 00:29:22.500
Then at the end of the planet,
you've counted up everything.

00:29:22.500 --> 00:29:25.670
He says, that's not the real
point, the real point is,

00:29:25.670 --> 00:29:30.670
the first ball, the first
juniper berry sized ball of mud

00:29:30.750 --> 00:29:33.930
is this mom of this life.

00:29:33.930 --> 00:29:35.830
And then there's the mom of this mom.

00:29:35.830 --> 00:29:37.260
And then there's a moms of that mom.

00:29:37.260 --> 00:29:38.260
And then there's the moms.

00:29:38.260 --> 00:29:41.920
So it's exponential. He's
saying, that's the real teaching.

00:29:41.920 --> 00:29:44.220
Because there is an end to the

00:29:44.220 --> 00:29:48.270
balls of juniper berry
sized balls in the planet.

00:29:48.270 --> 00:29:51.603
But there's no end, if you go exponential.

00:29:51.603 --> 00:29:54.027
SBYAR YANG, SKABS 'DIR
BLA MA'I GSUNG RGYUN LTAR

00:29:54.027 --> 00:29:55.750
KHA BSGYUR NAS

00:29:55.750 --> 00:29:58.970
If we adjust this statement by Nagarjuna

00:29:58.970 --> 00:30:01.970
to fit the oral tradition
around that statement.

00:30:01.970 --> 00:30:04.841
GSUNG RGYUN means oral tradition.

00:30:04.841 --> 00:30:07.113
KHA BSGYUR means if we adjust it

00:30:08.275 --> 00:30:13.025
SA CHEN PO 'DI RGYA SHUG GI
TSI GU TZAM GYI RIL BUR BYAS

00:30:17.230 --> 00:30:20.990
If we make tiny balls of mud

00:30:20.990 --> 00:30:23.820
equal in the size of juniper berries

00:30:23.820 --> 00:30:26.211
out of the whole planet,

00:30:26.211 --> 00:30:29.111
SA CHEN PO 'DI RANG GI TSE 'DI'I MA

00:30:30.945 --> 00:30:35.670
and then we say, this one
is my mother in this life,

00:30:35.670 --> 00:30:40.270
and the second ball is my
mother in the life before that,

00:30:40.270 --> 00:30:42.490
and a third ball is the mother

00:30:42.490 --> 00:30:45.823
I had in the life before the life before.

00:30:46.911 --> 00:30:47.744
RI LU RE

00:30:47.744 --> 00:30:49.319
Then if you put those balls,

00:30:49.319 --> 00:30:52.110
BZHAG means if you put them in a pile,

00:30:52.110 --> 00:30:54.076
RDZOGS TE

00:30:54.076 --> 00:30:55.090
you would reach an end.

00:30:55.090 --> 00:30:57.080
The planet would,

00:30:57.080 --> 00:31:01.862
the dirt in the planet would run out. But

00:31:01.862 --> 00:31:05.554
MA'I GRANGS KYI BRGYA STONG
GI CHAR YANG MI 'GRO BAS

00:31:05.554 --> 00:31:09.303
BRGYA CHA STONG CHA
means 1/100th or 1/1000th

00:31:09.303 --> 00:31:13.796
BRGYA CHA STONG CHA
means 1/100th or 1/1000th

00:31:13.796 --> 00:31:15.079
MI 'GRO

00:31:15.079 --> 00:31:20.062
It wouldn't represent 1/10th of 1%

00:31:20.062 --> 00:31:21.478
of your mothers you've had.

00:31:21.478 --> 00:31:23.550
You would run out of planet

00:31:23.550 --> 00:31:25.953
and you wouldn't reach

00:31:25.953 --> 00:31:30.935
0.001 of the mothers
you've had. Therefore,

00:31:30.935 --> 00:31:35.934
SEMS CAN THAMS CAD KYIS
MA MA BYAS NA MI 'DANG BA

00:31:36.943 --> 00:31:40.253
'DANG BA means to be sufficient.

00:31:40.253 --> 00:31:45.253
'O MA 'DANG GI 'DUG GAM means
do we have enough milk to

00:31:45.370 --> 00:31:46.503
give all the monks tea?

00:31:46.503 --> 00:31:49.610
'DANG means to be sufficient.

00:31:49.610 --> 00:31:54.610
He says you wouldn't have enough balls

00:31:54.780 --> 00:31:58.736
to represent all the
mothers. You would run out.

00:31:58.736 --> 00:31:59.819
It wouldn't--

00:32:01.733 --> 00:32:05.966
SEMS CAN KUN GYIS MA GRANGS
MED RE MA BYAS NA MI 'DANG BAS

00:32:07.420 --> 00:32:11.400
Unless every living being in the universe

00:32:11.400 --> 00:32:16.020
has been your mother countless times,

00:32:16.020 --> 00:32:17.793
the math doesn't work out.

00:32:18.820 --> 00:32:21.690
The math doesn't work out.

00:32:21.690 --> 00:32:25.110
The math is weird.

00:32:25.110 --> 00:32:28.500
Unless every living being
has been your mother,

00:32:28.500 --> 00:32:32.410
not once but countless times.

00:32:32.410 --> 00:32:36.676
SEMS CAN THAMS CAD KYIS
RANG GI MA BYAS SHING,

00:32:36.676 --> 00:32:40.826
RE RES KYANG MANG DU BYAS TE,
SEMS CAN 'DI'I LUS MA BLANGS

00:32:40.826 --> 00:32:45.434
BYA BA MED, BLANGS PA LA
GRANGS KYIS MI CHOD TSUL BSAM,

00:32:45.434 --> 00:32:49.010
SEMS CAN THAMS CAD KYIS RANG GI MA BYAS

00:32:49.010 --> 00:32:50.753
You got to be--

00:32:50.753 --> 00:32:53.190
So Tim, in this Lam Rim section,

00:32:53.190 --> 00:32:55.150
you have to be careful with the MAs,

00:32:55.150 --> 00:32:59.157
because generally they mean
not but here they mean mom.

00:32:59.157 --> 00:33:04.157
But some of them mean not so
you got to be careful. So here,

00:33:04.285 --> 00:33:07.070
SEMS CAN THAMS CAD KYIS RANG GI MA BYAS

00:33:07.070 --> 00:33:09.814
Every living being has been your mother.

00:33:09.814 --> 00:33:12.710
RE RES KYANG MANG DU BYAS TE

00:33:12.710 --> 00:33:16.217
And each one has been
your mom countless times.

00:33:16.217 --> 00:33:17.134
SEMS CAN 'DI'I LUS MA BLANGS BYA BA MED

00:33:19.080 --> 00:33:22.200
You cannot say there is a body

00:33:23.240 --> 00:33:26.100
of a life form that you have not taken.

00:33:26.100 --> 00:33:30.770
There's no lifeform's body,
which you have not lived in.

00:33:30.770 --> 00:33:35.430
You have dressed in the body
of every kind of insect,

00:33:35.430 --> 00:33:38.300
every kind of whale, every kind of bird,

00:33:38.300 --> 00:33:41.660
every kind of bacteria,
every kind of COVID virus.

00:33:41.660 --> 00:33:45.046
You have been.

00:33:45.046 --> 00:33:45.879
BLANGS BYA BA MED

00:33:45.879 --> 00:33:48.287
BLANGS PA LA GRANGS KYIS MI CHOD TSUL BSAM

00:33:48.287 --> 00:33:51.330
And there's no number.

00:33:51.330 --> 00:33:54.980
There's no count of how
many times you took on

00:33:54.980 --> 00:33:57.165
each of the different bodies.

00:33:57.165 --> 00:34:00.030
DE'ANG MI'I SKYE BA
BLANGS PA LTA BUR MTSON NA

00:34:00.030 --> 00:34:02.010
Then he says, you want to get deeper?

00:34:02.010 --> 00:34:02.987
You guys want to go deep?

00:34:02.987 --> 00:34:04.300
- [Students In Unison] Yes!

00:34:04.300 --> 00:34:08.350
He says, you've been every kind of bug

00:34:08.350 --> 00:34:12.520
countless times and
there's not enough mothers

00:34:12.520 --> 00:34:14.580
to be your mother for those bugs,

00:34:14.580 --> 00:34:18.260
unless it's been
everybody in the universe.

00:34:18.260 --> 00:34:20.330
The math doesn't work out.

00:34:20.330 --> 00:34:23.180
Moreover, DE'ANG, moreover,

00:34:23.180 --> 00:34:25.453
let's just talk about the
times you were born as a human.

00:34:25.453 --> 00:34:29.136
MI'I SKYE BA BLANGS PA LTA
BUR MTSON NA GLING 'DI'I SA

00:34:29.136 --> 00:34:31.440
PHYOGS 'DIR MA SKYES BYA BA MED

00:34:31.440 --> 00:34:35.990
You cannot point to a
square meter on this planet

00:34:35.990 --> 00:34:38.743
that you have not been
born, in that square meter.

00:34:41.190 --> 00:34:44.610
You cannot point to a
square meter in any country

00:34:44.610 --> 00:34:48.850
on the earth of this world,
where you have not been born.

00:34:48.850 --> 00:34:51.478
You cannot point to one.

00:34:51.478 --> 00:34:54.140
SKYES BYA BA MED, SKYES
PA LA GRANGS KYIS MI CHOD

00:34:54.140 --> 00:34:58.003
In fact, I don't know, pick
a place in Guadalajara.

00:34:59.480 --> 00:35:01.830
We talked about Aldo's neighborhood.

00:35:01.830 --> 00:35:05.490
The corner of the street
that Aldo lives on,

00:35:05.490 --> 00:35:10.490
that meter, you have been
born there countless times.

00:35:10.630 --> 00:35:12.500
You have been born in that square meter

00:35:12.500 --> 00:35:15.230
of this planet countless times.

00:35:15.230 --> 00:35:20.230
DE BZHIN DU SHAR LHO NUB BYANG

00:35:20.410 --> 00:35:22.830
East, South, West, North.

00:35:22.830 --> 00:35:24.030
I don't care what directions.

00:35:24.030 --> 00:35:27.620
I don't care what
country, forget countries.

00:35:27.620 --> 00:35:30.347
There's not a square inch where
you haven't been born before

00:35:30.347 --> 00:35:32.470
and countless times.

00:35:32.470 --> 00:35:35.540
And by the way, this world
only lasted, I don't know,

00:35:35.540 --> 00:35:37.410
5 billion years or something?

00:35:37.410 --> 00:35:38.243
It doesn't matter.

00:35:38.243 --> 00:35:41.000
He's talking about the
dirt that you were born on.

00:35:41.000 --> 00:35:43.840
You've been born on that dirt
countless times and that dirt

00:35:43.840 --> 00:35:47.953
has wandered around to different
planets countless times.

00:35:47.953 --> 00:35:49.790
'JIG RTEN RE RE LA'ANG GRANGS MED PA

00:35:49.790 --> 00:35:52.967
The worlds you have been
born on are countless.

00:35:52.967 --> 00:35:57.967
RE BLANGS PAS, SEMS CAN
LAS KYANG MANG BA'I PHYIR

00:35:57.980 --> 00:36:00.950
The number of planets you've
been born on countless times,

00:36:00.950 --> 00:36:05.130
exceeds the countless number of beings.

00:36:05.130 --> 00:36:07.300
Therefore, you have been everybody's kid

00:36:07.300 --> 00:36:09.680
countless times.

00:36:11.800 --> 00:36:15.383
I made this little
picture, you guys ready?

00:36:20.660 --> 00:36:24.250
I like this cute little
picture of our world.

00:36:24.250 --> 00:36:27.890
Somehow, I got it with
animals on it, which is cute.

00:36:27.890 --> 00:36:29.920
And then I like to read science fiction.

00:36:29.920 --> 00:36:31.580
I'm reading a science
fiction book right now

00:36:31.580 --> 00:36:34.990
about a trip to Sirius,
which is my next trip.

00:36:34.990 --> 00:36:38.230
It's a star that's not
too far away, blue star.

00:36:38.230 --> 00:36:41.710
And anyway, it's perro.

00:36:41.710 --> 00:36:44.550
It's the dog.

00:36:44.550 --> 00:36:47.880
I tried to put the stars.

00:36:47.880 --> 00:36:52.600
Imagine that this world
is located at each star

00:36:52.600 --> 00:36:56.770
and then imagine that you have been born

00:36:56.770 --> 00:36:59.800
in every corner of every planet,

00:36:59.800 --> 00:37:03.078
in every square meter of every planet.

00:37:03.078 --> 00:37:07.554
MA BYAS PA MA ZAD MI'I RTEN LA
AA MA MA BYAS PA'ANG MED PAS

00:37:08.680 --> 00:37:11.503
Not only has everyone been your mother,

00:37:11.503 --> 00:37:13.400
everyone's been your mother

00:37:13.400 --> 00:37:15.868
just in your human rebirth. Therefore,

00:37:15.868 --> 00:37:20.793
SEMS CAN THAMS CAD AA MA
CIS KYANG YIN SNYAM DU BSAM

00:37:22.267 --> 00:37:24.630
So it doesn't matter,

00:37:24.630 --> 00:37:28.600
AA MA CIS KYANG YIN, it doesn't
matter what they are now.

00:37:28.600 --> 00:37:32.490
Insect, virus, elephant,

00:37:32.490 --> 00:37:33.918
it doesn't matter.

00:37:33.918 --> 00:37:34.751
SNYAM DU BSAM

00:37:34.751 --> 00:37:36.944
Think about it, just think about it.

00:37:36.944 --> 00:37:38.920
DE LTAR BSAMS KYANG MA SKYES NA

00:37:38.920 --> 00:37:40.561
Then it's interesting, he says,

00:37:40.561 --> 00:37:41.911
DE LTAR BSAMS KYANG MA SKYES NA

00:37:41.911 --> 00:37:45.590
means look, if you do
all this logical flow

00:37:45.590 --> 00:37:49.449
I've been teaching you about
mothers and you don't get it,

00:37:49.449 --> 00:37:50.716
MA SKYES NA

00:37:50.716 --> 00:37:52.610
It's cute, he says, okay,

00:37:52.610 --> 00:37:54.640
everything I taught you today, forget it.

00:37:54.640 --> 00:37:56.930
If you don't get it, you
don't get it, what the heck?

00:37:56.930 --> 00:37:59.910
MA SKYES NA, I got another approach.

00:37:59.910 --> 00:38:01.929
I got another choice.

00:38:01.929 --> 00:38:04.560
RANG LA MA GTAN NAS MED DAM ZER NA

00:38:04.560 --> 00:38:07.527
Then he's, drop your hands
and he says, god damn,

00:38:07.527 --> 00:38:08.723
I'm starting to doubt

00:38:08.723 --> 00:38:11.710
whether I even had a mother in this life.

00:38:11.710 --> 00:38:15.900
Not only you don't get what
I'm trying to tell you,

00:38:15.900 --> 00:38:18.517
but you start to doubt your
own mother in this life.

00:38:18.517 --> 00:38:22.380
SKYE BA 'DI'I MA MNGON
SUM YOD SNYAM PA 'ONG BAS

00:38:22.380 --> 00:38:26.090
He says, go back to your mom in this life.

00:38:26.090 --> 00:38:29.510
You don't get all this logic.
It's too complicated for you.

00:38:29.510 --> 00:38:33.640
It's giving you a headache.
It's too convoluted. Okay.

00:38:33.640 --> 00:38:38.370
Let's go back to basics.

00:38:38.370 --> 00:38:40.780
Just go back to your mom in this life.

00:38:40.780 --> 00:38:42.640
You had a mom in this life, right?

00:38:42.640 --> 00:38:46.960
You can picture her,
maybe she's still alive.

00:38:46.960 --> 00:38:48.560
Let's just come back to there.

00:38:48.560 --> 00:38:51.283
When this meditation
gets too much for you,

00:38:52.430 --> 00:38:54.430
touchstone, go back to the touchstone,

00:38:54.430 --> 00:38:55.930
go back to your mom in this life.

00:38:55.930 --> 00:38:57.870
You can remember her face.

00:38:57.870 --> 00:39:00.610
You can remember beautiful
things she did for you.

00:39:00.610 --> 00:39:03.430
Just let's take it back
to your mom in this life.

00:39:03.430 --> 00:39:04.363
YOD SNYAM PA 'ONG BAS,

00:39:04.363 --> 00:39:07.638
DES SKYE BA 'DI'I SNGA MA
SOGS KYI MA LA SBYAR TE

00:39:07.638 --> 00:39:09.600
SPOGS CHOG BYA

00:39:09.600 --> 00:39:13.230
Then focus on her having been

00:39:13.230 --> 00:39:15.260
the mom in your previous life.

00:39:15.260 --> 00:39:16.330
Don't try to see

00:39:16.330 --> 00:39:18.740
all living beings have been your mom.

00:39:18.740 --> 00:39:22.000
You already have an attachment
to your mom in this life.

00:39:22.000 --> 00:39:24.110
So ride that attachment.

00:39:24.110 --> 00:39:26.070
Forget all the other living beings.

00:39:26.070 --> 00:39:28.110
Forget all the grasshoppers.

00:39:28.110 --> 00:39:30.669
Your mom in this life.

00:39:34.119 --> 00:39:35.785
- [Male Student] Saltamontes.

00:39:35.785 --> 00:39:38.010
- Saltamontes.

00:39:38.010 --> 00:39:41.970
If it's too much for you, just
take your mom in this life

00:39:41.970 --> 00:39:44.000
and imagine that maybe in a past life,

00:39:44.000 --> 00:39:45.880
she was also your mom. You can do that.

00:39:45.880 --> 00:39:47.909
That's not so hard.

00:39:47.909 --> 00:39:49.310
SBYAR TE SPOGS CHOG BYA

00:39:49.310 --> 00:39:52.335
SPOGS here, the word SPOGS means,

00:39:52.335 --> 00:39:54.076
RJES DPAG TSAD MA

00:39:54.076 --> 00:39:55.920
which means deduction.

00:39:55.920 --> 00:39:58.213
This is the verb and it's very unusual, so

00:39:58.213 --> 00:40:02.840
SPOGS means, use your logic.

00:40:02.840 --> 00:40:06.540
Use your logic, but don't
go to all the insects,

00:40:06.540 --> 00:40:09.970
whales and elephants, just go to this mom

00:40:09.970 --> 00:40:11.770
and she was your mom before.

00:40:11.770 --> 00:40:13.655
Can you handle that?
I can handle that.

00:40:17.690 --> 00:40:21.570
I love the next sentence
and it means a lot to me

00:40:21.570 --> 00:40:24.133
and we're going to close
with that sentence.

00:40:25.356 --> 00:40:27.650
MAR SHES BSGOM TSUL 'DI DAG

00:40:27.650 --> 00:40:32.650
Now this method of meditating on MAR SHES.

00:40:32.980 --> 00:40:35.477
What's MAR SHES?

00:40:35.477 --> 00:40:37.870
Realize, SHES means realize

00:40:37.870 --> 00:40:39.466
everyone's been your mom.

00:40:39.466 --> 00:40:40.980
MAR SHES BSGOM TSUL 'DI DAG

00:40:40.980 --> 00:40:45.980
This whole thing I taught
you in the last two days,

00:40:46.030 --> 00:40:50.840
about seeing that people
have been your mom,

00:40:50.840 --> 00:40:55.620
it's only presented briefly
in the classical Lam Rims.

00:40:55.620 --> 00:40:57.848
And he mentions two of them.

00:40:57.848 --> 00:40:59.580
BDE LAM, Path To Bliss,

00:40:59.580 --> 00:41:04.483
which, Venerable Gyelse, was written by?

00:41:04.483 --> 00:41:06.060
- I'm sorry, I wasn't paying attention.

00:41:06.060 --> 00:41:08.410
Nevermind.

00:41:08.410 --> 00:41:12.460
First Panchen Lama, 1565 - 1662,

00:41:12.460 --> 00:41:15.180
Panchen Lobsang Chukyi Gyelsen,

00:41:15.180 --> 00:41:18.190
which is part of the Diamond
Mountain advanced course

00:41:18.190 --> 00:41:21.200
for ACI, first three courses.

00:41:21.200 --> 00:41:25.000
That Lam Rim, and then
there's a commentary.

00:41:25.000 --> 00:41:28.380
There's a Lam Rim which is
like a commentary to it.

00:41:28.380 --> 00:41:31.800
Pabongka Rinpoche says,
like a commentary to it,

00:41:31.800 --> 00:41:34.665
by his Holiness the Second Panchen Lama,

00:41:34.665 --> 00:41:36.380
who is Lobsang Yeshe called MYUR LAM

00:41:36.380 --> 00:41:40.140
Which means, quick path, quick path.

00:41:40.140 --> 00:41:42.750
He says, look,

00:41:42.750 --> 00:41:46.320
if you go to those two classical Lam Rims,

00:41:46.320 --> 00:41:49.490
you won't find all these
arguments that I gave you.

00:41:49.490 --> 00:41:51.960
They just give a very brief presentation.

00:41:51.960 --> 00:41:53.670
Everyone's been your mother, it's logical

00:41:53.670 --> 00:41:55.380
and then go on.

00:41:55.380 --> 00:41:59.958
He says, so where did this
explanation come from?

00:41:59.958 --> 00:42:04.817
BDAG GIS BLA MA'I MDUN DU
DKA' BA SPYAD PA'I LAG RJES

00:42:04.817 --> 00:42:09.420
I spent a blank load of hours

00:42:09.420 --> 00:42:11.967
learning this from my teacher,

00:42:11.967 --> 00:42:16.967
and DKA' BA SPYAD PA means
and I worked my ass off.

00:42:17.430 --> 00:42:18.993
It was hard.

00:42:18.993 --> 00:42:22.770
DKA' BA SPYAD PA means I worked my ass off

00:42:22.770 --> 00:42:24.480
learning this from my lamas,

00:42:24.480 --> 00:42:27.843
for year after year,
after year, after year.

00:42:27.843 --> 00:42:31.990
LAG RJES means this is just the footprint

00:42:31.990 --> 00:42:34.440
of that effort.

00:42:34.440 --> 00:42:38.210
The presentation you heard
in the last two sessions

00:42:38.210 --> 00:42:43.210
is just the shadow or the sign of the

00:42:43.590 --> 00:42:46.800
thousands of hours I
spent learning this stuff

00:42:46.800 --> 00:42:48.930
and trying to understand this stuff.

00:42:48.930 --> 00:42:53.930
That's just the mere shadow
of the effort I put in.

00:42:54.113 --> 00:42:58.416
DKA' BA SPYAD means put in effort.

00:42:58.416 --> 00:43:03.250
MAN NGAG LTAR GYI SA BCAD
'DI RGYAS SU BTANG BA YIN PAS

00:43:03.250 --> 00:43:07.073
And I've written this presentation.

00:43:07.073 --> 00:43:11.270
SA BCAD 'DI means this
presentation or this outline

00:43:11.270 --> 00:43:14.979
of the logic for how many moms you've had.

00:43:14.979 --> 00:43:15.930
RGYAS SU BTANG BA YIN PAS

00:43:15.930 --> 00:43:20.790
I expanded on it based on the
thousands of hours I spent

00:43:20.790 --> 00:43:23.450
learning it from great teachers.

00:43:23.450 --> 00:43:27.977
I worked hard and I'm
offering it to you, free.

00:43:29.269 --> 00:43:32.130
RGYUN DU NYAMS LEN MDZAD MKHAN DANG

00:43:32.130 --> 00:43:35.050
If you're a person

00:43:35.050 --> 00:43:38.270
who's keeping up their Buddhist
practice pretty steadily,

00:43:38.270 --> 00:43:41.170
if you're the kind of person

00:43:41.170 --> 00:43:43.690
who's responsible about their practice--

00:43:43.690 --> 00:43:45.180
look, nobody's perfect,

00:43:45.180 --> 00:43:47.540
you're not keeping your Six Times book,

00:43:47.540 --> 00:43:48.560
you're meditating but you're not

00:43:48.560 --> 00:43:50.830
keeping your Six Times
book. Or you're doing yoga

00:43:50.830 --> 00:43:53.960
but you're not meditating.
Or you're, you know, come on,

00:43:53.960 --> 00:43:55.880
when can we do all those things?

00:43:55.880 --> 00:44:00.150
But he says, if you're a
pretty steady practitioner

00:44:00.150 --> 00:44:02.247
BSTAN PA'I KHUR BZHES PA

00:44:02.247 --> 00:44:07.247
This KHUR we discussed in the
Abhidharma class recently,

00:44:08.060 --> 00:44:10.340
because it was on an elephant

00:44:11.680 --> 00:44:15.430
and it related to the
84,000 heaps of dharma.

00:44:17.013 --> 00:44:20.680
KHUR means a load that
you put on an animal.

00:44:20.680 --> 00:44:24.890
Sometimes the number of

00:44:24.890 --> 00:44:27.310
teachings given by Lord Buddha is defined

00:44:27.310 --> 00:44:32.310
as the number of small books
you could load on an elephant

00:44:32.400 --> 00:44:36.290
the size of this
building, which is 84,000.

00:44:36.290 --> 00:44:37.540
Anyway, that's KHUR.

00:44:37.540 --> 00:44:38.760
Here, BSTAN PA'I KHUR BZHES PA.

00:44:40.130 --> 00:44:43.638
Are you the kind of person
who is going to take

00:44:43.638 --> 00:44:46.800
responsibility to keep
these teachings alive?

00:44:46.800 --> 00:44:50.280
Are you going to be an ALL Gold Club?

00:44:50.280 --> 00:44:52.486
I don't know what they call it in Mexico.

00:44:52.486 --> 00:44:53.640
- Club de Oro

00:44:53.640 --> 00:44:56.620
- A Gold Club or a Club de Oro.

00:44:56.620 --> 00:45:00.070
Are you going to be the kind of person

00:45:00.070 --> 00:45:03.620
who takes responsibility

00:45:03.620 --> 00:45:06.540
to make these teachings
survive on this planet?

00:45:06.540 --> 00:45:08.640
Are you going to join
all those gold clubs,

00:45:08.640 --> 00:45:11.280
and jade clubs, and club-clubs.

00:45:11.280 --> 00:45:15.200
And if you're the kind of person

00:45:15.200 --> 00:45:17.440
who keeps up a decent practice,

00:45:17.440 --> 00:45:21.310
not perfect. And if you're
the kind of person who says,

00:45:21.310 --> 00:45:24.600
I'm going to make sure these
teachings stay on this planet.

00:45:24.600 --> 00:45:28.150
I take responsibility.
I will raise money in

00:45:28.150 --> 00:45:30.420
Guadalajara.
It's tough in Guadalajara.

00:45:30.420 --> 00:45:32.730
It's not like New York.

00:45:32.730 --> 00:45:36.853
I take responsibility, if
you're that kind of person.

00:45:36.853 --> 00:45:38.580
PHYAG LEN

00:45:38.580 --> 00:45:42.540
I charge you, I give
you the responsibility,

00:45:42.540 --> 00:45:45.420
don't let this teaching get lost.

00:45:45.420 --> 00:45:50.270
I worked hard to learn
this from my teachers

00:45:50.270 --> 00:45:53.000
and I give you responsibility

00:45:53.000 --> 00:45:57.180
to don't let this mom teaching
get lost in the world.

00:45:57.180 --> 00:45:59.770
It's very beautiful. He's
like, please, please.

00:45:59.770 --> 00:46:04.180
I worked so hard to get it
straight, please keep it.

00:46:04.180 --> 00:46:06.320
Take care of it.

00:46:06.320 --> 00:46:08.710
This lama will go, that lama will go, but

00:46:08.710 --> 00:46:10.610
each generation has to say,

00:46:10.610 --> 00:46:12.860
yeah, I'll keep this mom logic.

00:46:12.860 --> 00:46:15.120
I'll be the mom logic keeper.

00:46:15.120 --> 00:46:16.800
The Gold Club of Guadalajara

00:46:16.800 --> 00:46:19.360
will be the mom logic keeper.

00:46:19.360 --> 00:46:21.054
I take responsibility.

00:46:21.054 --> 00:46:23.790
KHYAD CHE BA YOD means that's a big deal!

00:46:23.790 --> 00:46:26.243
That's a big deal, if you guys can do it.

00:46:27.400 --> 00:46:30.710
Keep this teaching,
this precious teaching,

00:46:30.710 --> 00:46:33.290
keep it well, because--

00:46:33.290 --> 00:46:34.705
Then I like the picture,

00:46:34.705 --> 00:46:39.705
we can close on the
picture of taking care.

00:46:39.750 --> 00:46:42.180
I don't know, me and
Pachi are working on this

00:46:43.290 --> 00:46:48.200
carbon sequestering--hey
I remembered the word--

00:46:48.200 --> 00:46:51.134
program and it's a big, big thing now.

00:46:51.134 --> 00:46:53.330
It's in all the newspapers now.

00:46:53.330 --> 00:46:57.410
Suddenly, I never saw sequester
before, now it's everywhere.

00:46:57.410 --> 00:47:02.410
Can we take care of these plants

00:47:02.800 --> 00:47:05.020
which will store that knowledge?

00:47:05.020 --> 00:47:06.830
And that's our responsibility.

00:47:06.830 --> 00:47:09.271
And so Pabongka Rinpoche is begging us,

00:47:09.271 --> 00:47:10.979
please take care.

00:47:10.979 --> 00:47:14.560
Please take responsibility
to take care of this

00:47:14.560 --> 00:47:16.610
mom logic teaching.

00:47:16.610 --> 00:47:19.218
So you guys, please,
also take responsibility

00:47:19.218 --> 00:47:21.643
and we'll see you in the next class.

